## Fixed

The first start in a new project printed a database line above the startup banner:

```
info  Applied database migrations count=3 versions=[1,2,3]
```

Migrations run before Mica has read your content model, and the banner cannot be written until it has. So on a first start, and only then, the log line came first — on the one start where the first line matters most.

Mica now asks for that announcement at debug level when the command runs it. A server log still records it at info level, where it belongs.
